join Sipho (Neutral) left
Zanele: Sipho. Would you do something for me.
Sipho: ...Now?
Zanele: Three mornings a week, the first hour. The younger ones.
Zanele: I am not doing you a kindness. I have thirty-four children and one of me, and you have just held four of them still for six minutes on the subject of gutters.
Zanele: That is a skill. I would like to borrow it.
- That was generous
	Hope: That was generous.
	Zanele: It was accurate.
	Zanele: Generous would be giving him something he could not do. I have given him something he is already better at than I was at his age, and I have got an hour back.
